From 97fe3db664e633b8bbfbc5633713e5f7435f6897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xjosemi <xjosemi@local>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:40:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] config: CONFIG_RCU_BOOST=y (como el Pixel 3a)

Mejora la latencia de RCU para tareas de alta prioridad. Es lo que usa el
kernel de CarbonROM para bonito/sargo (mismo SDM670, mismo 4.9).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Change-Id: Ic963cd40aa02f30753362aa42893ea780313e6e9
---
 arch/arm64/configs/gts4lv_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gts4lv_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gts4lv_defconfig
index 15a2bdbb7..a420db08d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gts4lv_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gts4lv_defconfig
@@ -815,3 +815,4 @@ CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_CRC32_ARM64=y
 CONFIG_XZ_DEC=y
 CONFIG_QMI_ENCDEC=y
+CONFIG_RCU_BOOST=y
-- 
2.49.0

